<p><strong>TL;DR</strong> =E2=80=94 Granite 4.1 is a family of dense, decod=
er=E2=80=91only LLMs (3B, 8B, and 30B) trained on ~15T tokens using a multi=
=E2=80=91stage pre=E2=80=91training pipeline, including long=E2=80=91contex=
t extension of up to 512K tokens. The models are further refined with super=
vised fine=E2=80=91tuning on ~4.1M high=E2=80=91quality curated samples and=
 reinforcement learning via on=E2=80=91policy GRPO with DAPO loss (<a href=
=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.14476" rel=3D"nofollow">Yu et al., 2025</a>)=
. Notably, the 8B instruct model matches or surpasses the previous Granite =
4.0=E2=80=91H=E2=80=91Small (32B=E2=80=91A9B MoE) despite using a simpler d=
ense architecture with fewer parameters. All Granite 4.1 models are release=
d under the Apache 2.0 license.</p>
