<p>Building high=E2=80=91quality small language models goes beyond simply s=
caling compute=E2=80=94it requires rigorous data curation throughout traini=
ng. For Granite 4.1, we prioritized data quality over quantity, progressive=
ly refining the data mixture across five pre=E2=80=91training stages. We fu=
rther curated supervised fine=E2=80=91tuning data using an LLM=E2=80=91as=
=E2=80=91Judge framework and applied a multi=E2=80=91stage reinforcement le=
arning pipeline to systematically strengthen performance in math, coding, i=
nstruction following, and general chat.</p>
