	<span>
		Training Methodology
	</span>
</h3>
<p>We use <strong>On-policy GRPO (Group Relative Policy Optimization)</stro=
ng> (<a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.03300" rel=3D"nofollow">Shao et =
al., 2024</a>) with <strong>DAPO (Decoupled Clip and Dynamic sAmpling Polic=
y Optimization) loss</strong> (<a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.14476"=
 rel=3D"nofollow">Yu et al., 2025</a>) which provides more stable training =
signals compared to standard GRPO. However, due to computationally intensiv=
e nature of dynamic sampling, we switch it off during our training runs.</p=
>
